Sink The task returns Written <code>table_sink(table, columns=...)</code> A row (dict), or a list of them Into a table of the project <code>graph_sink(nodes=..., relations=...)</code> <code>{node: rows}</code> Into several tables, the keys of one row filled into the others <code>file_sink(path, fmt=...)</code> Text, bytes, or anything as JSON Into a file under the project: one at the end, one that grows (<code>append=True</code>) or one per group (<code>per_batch=True</code>) <pre><code>from ms_flow import file_sink


@task()
def describe(value: int) -&gt; str:
    return f"{value}\t{value * value}\n"


@job(task=describe, output=file_sink("squares.tsv", fmt="text", append=True))
def squares(params, project):
    yield from range(10)
</code></pre> <p>Each group of results is written in one transaction, on the engine's delivery thread, and an element counts as done once its results are in. The tables must exist: the app creates them.</p> <p>A job may write its results itself: <code>output</code> is then a function <code>(params, project)</code> that returns an object with <code>write(results)</code> and, optionally, <code>finish()</code> and <code>tables</code>. <code>writer(sink, project)</code> gives the writer of a sink, for one that changes the results before a sink writes them.</p>
